# Pipeline-generated output (regenerated every run; authoritative copy lives on the
# `data-sync` branch, which is Vercel's Production Branch). Committing these to `main`
# caused a real production incident: main's copy went stale and Vercel's Git
# integration deployed it, silently overriding fresher CLI/data-sync deploys. See
# PROJECT_REVIEW.md DEV-27. Hand-maintained config (booster_collation_overrides.json,
# product_overrides.json) and non-pipeline static data (precon_decks.json,
# booster_slots.json, scryfall_set_hierarchy.json) are NOT ignored and must stay tracked.
public/data/sets.json
public/data/sealed_products.json
public/data/booster_ev.json
public/data/arbitrage_leaderboard.json
public/data/single_card_prices.json
public/data/pricing_reliability.json
